{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MDbaG5bSQ349XfpsfrzrNR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what Anchor is, grounded in the project docs:\n\n- **It's a personal productivity / task-management system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain markdown files as the single source of truth** â€” DASHBOARD.md, PROJECTS.md, INBOX.md, domain files (academic/commercial/family/writing), plus archives (CANCELLED.md, SAVED_FOR_LATER.md). No database, no syncing.\n\n- **It ships as a self-contained local web app** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders a fully interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs persistently as the **NSSM Windows service `anchor`**. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task workflow:** tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored, each with priority, energy, domain, due date, and notes; managed via dashboard clicks or CLI commands (`done`, `add`, `capture`, `cancel`, `save`, `restore`).\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\"** layered on top â€” a per-project cockpit for running the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman trio** (research/plan/build skills) as durable, server-side sessions. This has shipped through four versions:\n  - **v2:** session model, cached/validated summaries, Grass-Catchers idea lane, deliverable pinning, an interactive stream-json REPL terminal.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\":** real ConPTY terminals (the one declared `pywinpty` exception to the stdlib-only rule), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, proactive cached project summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (always on a port â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built + merged to master 2026-06-13, 9 waves GREEN, 637 tests): one terminal substrate that auto-loads the lane's skill once and greets once (fixing the repeating-prompt bug), a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, Paradigm-2 inline expanding panels, per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-to-lane promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **It self-verifies daily:** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint, and walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching the real `:8777` service), then writing a dated health report.\n\n- **Hard constraint it holds to:** Python stdlib only (the lone exception being optional `pywinpty` for terminals), no binary/compiled assets, every file remaining readable by any CLI tool â€” enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21d341f1-9956-48c0-8f34-7b4a3be52d9c","uuid":"62463549-ed56-4f39-91d5-51f27f267454","request_id":"req_011Cc1XvXw2eLSD4C7Ny7CmY"}
